: 2, "correct_feedback": "Correct!", "attempt_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}, {"type": "text", "content": ""}], "incorrect_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "Whoops! Something important is missing."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Maybe next time..."}]}}, {"type": "post_instructions", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Instructions: Complete the following steps. Fill in the Self Assessment."}]}, {"type": "learning_skills", "contents": [{"type": "skill", "content": "Reading"}, {"type": "skill", "content": "Writing"}, {"type": "skill", "content": "Speaking"}]}]}], "type": "scholar", "_data": [{"type": "lab_options", "contents": [{"type": "has_nav", "content": true}, {"type": "has_exercise_controls", "content": true}]}], "id": 0, "stimuli": [{"type": "welcome", "template_override": 1, "_data": [], "id": 0, "contents": [{}]}, {"contents": [{"type": "slideshow", "value": {"coverimg": "engenn9le09ob01re2img01.jpg", "audiosrc": "engenn9le09ob01re2aud01", "images": [{"time": "0", "image": "engenn9le09ob01re2img01.jpg", "text": "", "id": 0}, {"time": "100", "image": "engenn9le09ob01re2img01.jpg", "text": "After the strike, the workers finally won and everything was back to normal; except, it wasn't. Management decided to keep some scab workers on the team. They even had the gall to move a few into management positions. Many people were appalled at management's short-sightedness to do something so petty. That is when I decided to take the buy-out package and leave the company.", "id": 1}, {"time": "25000", "image": "engenn9le09ob01re2img02.jpg", "text": "If management hadn't hired on scab workers, I would have stayed. In my opinion, they want the more experienced workers gone, so they can hire younger, cheaper ones. I think in five years, there will be a completely new staff  there and in five years, all of the former employees will be working somewhere else.", "id": 2}, {"time": "43000", "image": "engenn9le09ob01re2img03.jpg", "text": "It's a shame we went on strike. If we had talked to management more, we could have worked out our problems. If we had taken some extra time to listen to each other, the strike wouldn't have happened. However, it did, and now I find myself looking for a new job, but this time it will be different. This time I will find a job that I love and that I am passionate about. If I had followed my dreams earlier, I wouldn't have gotten myself into this mess. No bother,  I give myself five months. In five months, I will be working in the job I want. In four months, I will be working in a job that I can build a career from. These are exciting times.", "id": 3}]}}], "template_override": 1, "title": "", "type": "audio", "id": 1, "_data": []}]}], "_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "Getting the Job You Want"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Just Getting By"}, {"type": "position", "content": 1}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 9}, {"type": "level", "content": "B2.1"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Describe hypothetical situations in written and spoken interactions according to work and social contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear."}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear. "}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear. "}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Understands general and detailed information as well as attitude and intention on a wide range of general and work topics, in conversations or presentations, spoken at a natural speed and in circumstances that make it more difficult to hear. "}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "The Future Tense vs. The Future Continuous Tense"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use the Future tense (<span class=\"italic\">will</span>) to talk about a one-time action in the future.  <br/>You use the Future Continuous tense to talk about something happening (in progress) at a particular time in the future."}, {"type": "text", "content": "You use will to talk about a future action or event."}, {"type": "text", "content": "For example:<br/><span class=\"italic\">I think in five years, there <span class=\"strong\">will be</span> a completely new staff there.</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "When you use the Future Continuous tense, the action will have started before that moment but it will not have finished at that moment. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "For example:<br/><span class=\"italic\">I <span class=\"strong\">will be working</span> at 4 p.m. tomorrow. </span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "The person will start work at some point in the future and be working at 4 p.m. It is not clear when the person will stop working. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\">All of the former employees will be working somewhere else. </span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "The structure of the Future Continuous is:<br/> Subject + <span class=\"italic\">will</span> + <span class=\"italic\">be</span> + verb <span class=\"italic\">-ing</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\">In five months, I <span class=\"strong\">will be working</span> in the job I want.</span>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "In five months, I will be working in the job I want. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "In four months, I will be working in a job that I can build a career from."}, {"type": "example", "content": "I think in five years, there will be a completely new staff  there and in five years, all of the former employees will be working somewhere else. "}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "The Third Conditional"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "There are four types of conditional sentences in English:<ol><li>Zero Conditional - to talk about certainty and facts</li><li>First Conditional - to talk about real possibilities in the present or the future</li><li>Second Conditional - to talk about <span class=\"italic\">unreal</span> possibilities in the present or the future</li><li>Third Conditional - to talk about unreal <span class=\"italic\">past</span> situations</li></ol>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "You use third conditional to talk about unreal situations in the past. <br/>These are things that did not happen in the past. You often use the third conditional to talk about regrets."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Look at the chart below for the structure of the third conditional:"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":2,\"columns\":3,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\">Conditional Name</div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\">Structure</div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\">Example</div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Third \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">If</span> + Past Perfect, <span class=\\\"italic\\\">could</span>/<span class=\\\"italic\\\">would have</span> + past participle\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">If we had <span class=\\\"strong\\\">talked to</span> management more, we <span class=\\\"strong\\\">could have worked out</span> our problems. </span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}"}, {"type": "example", "content": "If management hadn't hired on scab workers, I would have stayed. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "If we had talked to management more, we could have worked out our problems. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "If we had taken some extra time to listen to each other, the strike wouldn't have happened."}, {"type": "example", "content": "If I had followed my dreams earlier, I wouldn't have gotten myself into this mess."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "scab"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "strike breaker"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Management decided to keep some scab workers on the team."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le09ob01aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you hear when you talk about chasing your dream job."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "buy-out"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the purchase in a company"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I decided to take the buy-out package and leave the company."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le09ob01aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "gall"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "imprudent"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: They even had the gall to move a few into management positions."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le09ob01aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "petty"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "of little importance; trivial."}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Many people were appalled at management's short-sightedness to do something so petty."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le09ob01aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "short-sightedness"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "suffering of miopia"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Many people were appalled at management's short-sightedness to do something so petty."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le09ob01aud05"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "no bother"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to express disagreement"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: No bother,  I give myself five months."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le09ob01aud06"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "strike"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a stoppage of activity to force an employer or some authority to agree to demands"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: After the strike, the workers finally won and everything was back to normal; except, it wasn't."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn9le09ob01aud07"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Go online or to the library to find out about an interesting job you would like to do."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Find out what it is and what they do."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Explain why it is interesting to you."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Write 200 words giving the full information in your own words."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Try to use Future Continuous and Future tense to discuss career plans and career goals."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Read your writing to a partner."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Discuss your job with them and exchange ideas."}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I find out about an interesting job."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I write about it in a 200 words giving information and details."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I use Future tense and Future Continuous tense to talk about my job. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "I share my ideas and ask my partner for his or her opinion of my job."}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn9le09ob01re1img01.jpg"}]}